  "title": "Kueper2024: Unilateral vs bilateral movement-execution EEG dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 8 healthy participants performing self-initiated, self-paced reaching movements, either unilateral (right arm) or bilateral (both arms). Data were recorded with a 64-channel wireless active-electrode system and support movement intention recognition for exoskeleton-supported stroke rehabilitation. This BIDS release was re-formatted via MOABB from the original Zenodo deposit.",
  "methods_description": "64-channel EEG (extended 10-20 montage, Brain Products LiveAmp64, Acticap slim active electrodes) was sampled at 500 Hz with FCz reference and AFz ground. Hardware prefiltering was 0.1-131 Hz. Each subject performed 3 sets of 40 self-initiated movements per condition (unilateral button press, bilateral synchronous), giving 6 runs per subject.",
